 "about_text": "Good Mother Gallery was founded in Oakland in 2014 and is now anchored in Los Angeles' West Adams district, while maintaining its original Oakland space. The gallery focuses on California's contemporary art scene, presenting monthly exhibitions of artists it describes as risk-takers, spanning emerging and established practices. Beyond its exhibition program, Good Mother Gallery curates offsite projects and public art initiatives, drawing on a decade of experience in civic art collaborations. It is a member of the New Art Dealers Alliance (NADA) and the Gallery Association Los Angeles (GALA), and works with artists nationally and internationally to build collector relationships and artist careers.",
